📈 Key Insights
Houses with more rooms generally command higher market values.
Higher crime rates are associated with lower property prices.
Neighborhood socio-economic conditions significantly influence housing demand.
Accessibility to employment centers positively impacts property values.
Tax rates and education-related indicators also contribute to pricing differences.
